    "video": {
      "name": "Keto Turkey Meatballs [with Zoodles]",
      "description": "This heavenly dinner meal will be a treat for any table: fried turkey meatballs bursting with flavor are covered with a deliciously savory tomato sauce and placed over a bed of fresh and tender zucchini noodles. This meal is tasty, full of nutrition, and filling while not feeling too heavy—it has all the bonuses of noodles without any of the drawbacks! If you’re craving a delicious health kick, read on.\n\nZucchini is a go-to in the keto lifestyle, and for good reason: it’s low in carbs, fat, and sugar, but packed full of the good stuff like antioxidants and nutrients. It’s also easy to cook in many forms for succulent deliciousness: zoodles are an excellent example. Use a spiralizer to noodle-ify your zucchinis, boil to al dente tenderness, and drizzle with olive oil. Healthy comfort food has never been easier or more delicious!\n\nZoodles are fantastic, but the real star of this show is the moist homemade turkey meatballs, smothered lavishly in a rustic roasted garlic and sundried tomato sauce. Turkey is an excellent source of nutrients, vitamins, and protein. In saying that, feel free to swap out your meat with pork, chicken, beef, or whatever suits your personal preference.\n\nSo if you thought low-carb meant no more Italian cuisine, think again! This dish elicits all the classic savory goodness of a classic meatballs-and-pasta meal while remaining entirely keto-friendly. Perfect for a cozy night in or a big lunch, this recipe is sure to become a new favorite.\n\nRead the full recipe with full nutrition breakdown and step-by-step pictures over at:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nIngredients:\nGround Turkey:\n24 ounce ground turkey\n1/4 cup mayonnaise\nSalt and pepper to taste\n1 teaspoon onion powder\n3 tablespoon olive oil\n\nZoodles & Tomato Sauce:\n1 1/2 cup Rao’s low carb tomato sauce\n2 tablespoon olive oil\nSalt and pepper to taste\n24 ounce spiralized zucchini\n1/2 cup parmesan cheese, shredded\n1/4 cup fresh basil, chopped\n\nNutrition Summary: This makes a total of 4 servings of Keto Turkey Meatballs and Zoodles. Each serving comes out to be 785 calories, 77.6g fat, 7.8g net carbs, and 50.7g protein.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSee more keto recipes, knowledge and tips on the website to keep your weight loss going strong.\n\nEverything you need to know about the keto diet:\n\nGetting started? Everything you need is here:\n\nWe also make things easy with this 14 day diet plan:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFollow Ruled.Me for more tasty food:",
